Sedecium is a people and a service from beyond the [[Phenomena/Firmament|firmament]], at war with the [[Divinity/Thessians|Thessians]], the cadre of beings that seek to end all life in the universe. Its people mark themselves and their works with a sixteen-pointed star, the same mark that shows on the hull of the [[Geography/Færrin/Infinite Horizon/Far Realms/Hesperid|Hesperid]] and, at [[Geography/Færrin/Infinite Horizon/Far Realms/Hesperid 3|Hesperid 3]], as a triangle of sixteen dots. They reckon their history from a founding, or a second founding, and count the present year as 72.

Their home is [[Geography/Ushas/index|Ushas]], very far from [[Geography/Færrin/index|Færrin]]. They travel between worlds and keep both a military command and a corps of trained liaisons; a liaison's rite of suppression gives an anomaly life so that it can be fought and killed. They have long tracked the Thessians, and know several by name and shape. A Sedecium crew chased [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Esoterica|Gremory]] across the void on the eve of his ascension and ran their ship into him to stop it, a move that failed. They know [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Pyre|Pyre]], [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Herald|Herald]] and [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Giant|Giant]] as Thessians, and know [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Esoterica|Esoterica]], [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/War|War]] and [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Regent|Regent]] as the fourth-generation Thessians Gremory, Astaroth and Paimon. The only way they know to kill one of them is a spike of a [[Phenomena/Holy Gold|rare gold metal]]. In the open space between worlds they keep citadels of steel, one of them [[Geography/Elysium|Elysium]], where their people rest and trade between spheres.

Sedecium grew out of a wreck in the Far Realms of [[Geography/Ushas/index|Ushas]], a different place from the [[Geography/Færrin/Infinite Horizon/Far Realms/index|Far Realms]] on Færrin's Infinite Horizon. A starship of the [[Org/The Fifth Prosperous Empire of the Sundom|Fifth Sundom]] had crashed there long before, and its survivors, pear-shaped people patterned in black and white, had regressed in the years since. The founders found a [[Bestiary/Kaathe|Kaathe]] construct in the wreckage, and Sedecium started out of what they took from it.

Sedecium began as a single crystal shell offering and has grown into a hegemony of fourteen or fifteen member systems, strung along the outer rim of the [[Geography/index|Astra]] where it stays clear of the prying eye of the [[Divinity/Thessians|Thessians]]. Its three founders have gone down in history: [[People/Dorcan|Dorcan]], who is a god, and [[People/Zugg|Zugg]] and [[People/Rodic|Rodic]], who live on. Rather than go into the crowded interior of the Astra in person, it keeps a large information network and reads the patterns in what it gathers. Chief among those patterns is the one it calls the entity, an unobservable presence that has dogged it for its whole history and leads it to weapons, lost systems and new allies. The entity is [[People/Althane/The Broker|Tech]]. When [[Phenomena/The Pale|the Pale]] consumed the old landmasses of Ushas, Sedecium moved the whole of its people to new ground, in [[Geography/Ushas/New Volcantum|New Volcantum]]. Sedecium holds that beings made by craft are people, and makes them where it needs them.

It keeps forward operating bases in quiet corners of the Astra, small stations from which it watches a region and runs its missions. When a job is too large for those, it empties a base to crew a ship and throws many fire teams of three at the problem, expecting only a handful to succeed. Its people are immortal and keep backups of themselves with their loved ones, so the dead can be rebooted, losing about a day of memory and whatever they carried. It hunts the Thessians for what their bodies hold, and refits old [[Org/The Fifth Prosperous Empire of the Sundom|Sundom]] craft to its own war.
